(window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS=window.XZ_MANUAL_CHAPTERS||{})["screen-and-themes"]="<header class=\"mc-head\"><p class=\"mc-eyebrow\">MODS menu<\/p><h2 class=\"mc-title\" tabindex=\"-1\">Screen, interfaces and themes<\/h2><p class=\"mc-lede\">MODERN or CLASSIC, the 25 themes, waveform colours, key notation, deck view and the play screen's parts.<\/p><p class=\"applies\" data-applies=\"both\">Applies to <b>MODERN and CLASSIC<\/b><\/p><\/header><p>SCREEN is the MODS section for how the player looks. Here you choose between the MODERN and CLASSIC interfaces, pick a theme, set the waveform colours and the 3-band colours, and decide how keys are written. Nothing on this page changes how a track sounds.<\/p>\n<p>Open MODS with <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span>, then choose <strong>SCREEN<\/strong> in the section rail.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-the-screen-page\" data-anchor=\"the-screen-page\">The SCREEN page<\/h3>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · SCREEN<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/cb5c523ef44bb366.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The SCREEN page with CLASSIC chosen. Under MODERN, the THEME row reads LAMPS AND TITLES, 3-BAND COLOURS sits beside it, and WAVEFORM COLOURS offers four choices.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/95a1b2af251c609a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The SCREEN page with CLASSIC chosen. Under MODERN, the THEME row reads LAMPS AND TITLES, 3-BAND COLOURS sits beside it, and WAVEFORM COLOURS offers four choices.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"31.250\" data-y=\"11.042\" aria-label=\"1: INTERFACE\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"58.750\" data-y=\"11.042\" aria-label=\"2: DECK VIEW\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"41.250\" data-y=\"33.958\" aria-label=\"3: THEME\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"84.375\" data-y=\"33.958\" aria-label=\"4: 3-BAND COLOURS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"37.500\" data-y=\"40.833\" aria-label=\"5: WAVEFORM COLOURS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"77.500\" data-y=\"40.833\" aria-label=\"6: KEY NOTATION\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"43.125\" data-y=\"60.833\" aria-label=\"7: PLAYING KEY\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"86.875\" data-y=\"60.833\" aria-label=\"8: KEY MATCH COLOURS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-8\">8<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"9\" data-x=\"43.125\" data-y=\"70.417\" aria-label=\"9: KEY BEFORE TITLE\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-9\">9<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"10\" data-x=\"90.000\" data-y=\"70.417\" aria-label=\"10: TRACK LIST COLUMNS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-10\">10<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"11\" data-x=\"50.000\" data-y=\"80.000\" aria-label=\"11: SYSTEM READOUT\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-11\">11<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"12\" data-x=\"90.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"12: WORKS ON\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-12\">12<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The SCREEN page with CLASSIC chosen. Under MODERN, the THEME row reads LAMPS AND TITLES, 3-BAND COLOURS sits beside it, and WAVEFORM COLOURS offers four choices.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>INTERFACE<\/b> <span>MODERN or CLASSIC. The framed picture is the one in use.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>DECK VIEW<\/b> <span>How many decks the play screen shows and in what order. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a>.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>THEME<\/b> <span>Opens CLASSIC THEMES. The value is the theme in use. Under MODERN this row is LAMPS AND TITLES.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>3-BAND COLOURS<\/b> <span>Opens the 3-BAND COLOURS page. The three squares are the colours of the lows, mids and highs now.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>WAVEFORM COLOURS<\/b> <span>How the scrolling waveforms are coloured.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>KEY NOTATION<\/b> <span>How keys are written everywhere MODS draws them.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>PLAYING KEY<\/b> <span>Shows the key a track plays in after tempo and key shift.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>KEY MATCH COLOURS<\/b> <span>Colours keys by how well they mix with the master deck.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"9\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-9\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">9<\/span><div><b>KEY BEFORE TITLE<\/b> <span>Shows the key in front of each title in the track list.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"10\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-10\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">10<\/span><div><b>TRACK LIST COLUMNS<\/b> <span>Tells you where to change the columns of the track list.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"11\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-11\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">11<\/span><div><b>SYSTEM READOUT<\/b> <span>CPU, memory and temperature on the top bar. Reads SET UP until you have run its setup.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"12\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-1-12\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">12<\/span><div><b>WORKS ON<\/b> <span>The decks the highlighted control applies to, in mixer order 3 1 2 4.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Control<\/th><th>Choices<\/th><th>What it changes<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>INTERFACE<\/td><td>CLASSIC, MODERN<\/td><td>Who draws the play screen. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\" data-anchor=\"modern-and-classic\">MODERN and CLASSIC<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>DECK VIEW<\/td><td>2 DECKS, 4 DECKS in number order, 4 DECKS in mixer order<\/td><td>Which decks the play screen shows. Sound and controls do not change. Hidden on a player that cannot run decks 3 and 4<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>THEME (CLASSIC)<\/td><td>24 classic themes<\/td><td>The look of the player's own screen and of MODS<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LAMPS AND TITLES (MODERN)<\/td><td>A page of switches<\/td><td>Which parts of the MODERN play screen you see<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3-BAND COLOURS<\/td><td>A page of colours<\/td><td>The colours of the lows, mids and highs in every 3-BAND waveform. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\" data-anchor=\"3-band-colours\">3-band colours<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>WAVEFORM COLOURS<\/td><td>STOCK, 3-BAND, STEMS (MODERN adds RGB)<\/td><td>The colours of the scrolling waveforms<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>KEY NOTATION<\/td><td>AS ON THE USB, MUSICAL, WHEEL<\/td><td>How keys are written<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>PLAYING KEY<\/td><td>ON, OFF<\/td><td>The key a track plays in now, or its original key<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>KEY MATCH COLOURS<\/td><td>ON, OFF<\/td><td>Green or amber keys on the play screen and in the track list<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>KEY BEFORE TITLE<\/td><td>ON, OFF<\/td><td>The key in front of each title in the track list<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TRACK LIST COLUMNS<\/td><td>Information only<\/td><td>Tap a column title in the track list, or press <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"menu\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/menu.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"60.86\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">MENU<\/span><\/span> there, to choose its columns and sort<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>SYSTEM READOUT<\/td><td>Opens its setup<\/td><td>CPU, RAM and temperature on the top bar. It has the last row of the page to itself<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The HOME card for SCREEN sums the page up in one line, for example <strong>Classic | 3-band | Am keys<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-modern-and-classic\" data-anchor=\"modern-and-classic\">MODERN and CLASSIC<\/h3>\n<p>XZ Mods gives the player two interfaces. You choose one with <strong>INTERFACE<\/strong> on the SCREEN page, or when you prepare the USB in the XZ Mods app. MODERN is the default.<\/p>\n<ul><li><strong>MODERN<\/strong> is a full-screen layout drawn by XZ Mods, with bigger waveforms and a browse sidebar.<\/li><li><strong>CLASSIC<\/strong> keeps the player's own play screen and adds MODS to it. The classic themes restyle that screen.<\/li><\/ul>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th><\/th><th>MODERN<\/th><th>CLASSIC<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Play screen<\/td><td>Drawn by XZ Mods, full screen<\/td><td>The XDJ-XZ's own layout, restyled<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Themes<\/td><td>One look, STANDARD. MODS is drawn in FLAGSHIP<\/td><td>24 themes. MODS is drawn in the theme you pick<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Waveform colours<\/td><td>STOCK, RGB, 3-BAND, STEMS<\/td><td>STOCK, 3-BAND, STEMS<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Lamps and titles<\/td><td>Each part can be shown or hidden<\/td><td>Not available<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Playing key<\/td><td>Shown as the big key in each deck's column<\/td><td>Shown where the beat countdown sits<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Stem buttons<\/td><td>Six places, including small buttons beside the hot cues<\/td><td>Five places<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Browse<\/td><td>The XZ Mods browser with a sidebar. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"browse\">Browsing and loading<\/a><\/td><td>The player's own browser<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Each interface keeps its own theme. If you switch from CLASSIC to MODERN and back, your classic theme comes back with you.<\/p>\n<p>To switch without opening MODS, press the <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"rekordbox\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/rekordbox.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"92.16\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">rekordbox<\/span><\/span> button above <span class=\"xzb\" data-key=\"link\"><img class=\"xzb-g\" src=\"assets/buttons/link.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"54.02\" height=\"32\"><span class=\"xzb-n\">LINK<\/span><\/span>. Out of the box it switches between MODERN and CLASSIC. You can give it another job in <strong>PLAY<\/strong> › <strong>REKORDBOX BUTTON<\/strong>. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"hardware\">Controls on the player<\/a>.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-2\" data-iface=\"modern\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODERN play screen<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The MODERN play screen with two decks, 3-BAND waveforms and the playing key shown.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"20.625\" data-y=\"7.083\" aria-label=\"1: Mode lamps\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"30.375\" data-y=\"62.500\" aria-label=\"2: QUANTIZE lamp\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"8.750\" data-y=\"21.875\" aria-label=\"3: Playing key\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"86.250\" data-y=\"12.500\" aria-label=\"4: Scrolling waveform\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"89.125\" data-y=\"7.083\" aria-label=\"5: STEMS and MODS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-5\">5<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The MODERN play screen with two decks, 3-BAND waveforms and the playing key shown.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Mode lamps<\/b> <span>SINGLE or CONTINUE, A. HOT CUE and A. CUE. Hide them in LAMPS AND TITLES.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>QUANTIZE lamp<\/b> <span>Red while QUANTIZE is on, with its beat value. Hide it in LAMPS AND TITLES.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Playing key<\/b> <span>The key the track plays in now. ORIGINAL below it is the key it was analysed in.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Scrolling waveform<\/b> <span>Coloured by WAVEFORM COLOURS.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-2-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>STEMS and MODS<\/b> <span>STEMS steps the stem buttons through their places, or shows and hides them in 4 DECKS. MODS opens the MODS menu.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<h3 id=\"m-classic-themes\" data-anchor=\"classic-themes\" data-iface=\"classic\">Classic themes <span class=\"tag tag--classic\">classic<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>A classic theme restyles the player's own play screen and the MODS menu: artwork, text, waveforms, cue marks and dialogs. Track positions, numbers and touch areas stay where the player puts them, so a theme never moves a control under your finger.<\/p>\n<p>Choose <strong>THEME<\/strong> on the SCREEN page to open <strong>CLASSIC THEMES<\/strong>. Tap a theme, or turn the encoder to it and push. Close MODS to see the play screen in the new theme.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-3\" data-iface=\"classic\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">CLASSIC THEMES<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/75a7223e70cba2ba.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Every classic theme on one page. ORIGINAL is in use.\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"16.250\" data-y=\"13.333\" aria-label=\"1: Theme in use\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-3-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"28.500\" data-y=\"12.500\" aria-label=\"2: Colour dots\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-3-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"33.125\" data-y=\"92.500\" aria-label=\"3: Dock\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-3-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"90.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"4: WORKS ON\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-3-4\">4<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Every classic theme on one page. ORIGINAL is in use.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-3-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>Theme in use<\/b> <span>Framed, with SELECTED under its name.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-3-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>Colour dots<\/b> <span>The theme's main colours, so you can compare themes before you pick one.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-3-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Dock<\/b> <span>Says what a theme restyles before you choose it.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-3-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>WORKS ON<\/b> <span>Themes apply to decks 1 to 4.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<p>The gallery shows the HOME page of MODS in every theme.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-4\" data-iface=\"classic\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/6953688aa006c458.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Original\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6953688aa006c458.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Original<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/6a122009269288ec.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: White\"><img src=\"manual/shots/6a122009269288ec.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>White<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/58266f58a4af7bef.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Cyberpunk\"><img src=\"manual/shots/58266f58a4af7bef.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Cyberpunk<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/9be6ea9882b24be9.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Neon\"><img src=\"manual/shots/9be6ea9882b24be9.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Neon<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/1c22b5b51250f8f3.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Mocha\"><img src=\"manual/shots/1c22b5b51250f8f3.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Mocha<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/71080343fbce8774.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Aurora\"><img src=\"manual/shots/71080343fbce8774.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Aurora<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/30f698cbb71a43e7.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Sandstone\"><img src=\"manual/shots/30f698cbb71a43e7.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Sandstone<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/ba742c9336a7dfa4.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Game Boy\"><img src=\"manual/shots/ba742c9336a7dfa4.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Game Boy<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/b7c868ed12b873c5.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Super Nintendo\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b7c868ed12b873c5.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Super Nintendo<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/2e1dc63452fd8fd6.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Windows 95\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2e1dc63452fd8fd6.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Windows 95<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/f5f836fa8f20d95a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Game Boy Color\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f5f836fa8f20d95a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Game Boy Color<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/312395099c0ecaa2.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Aqua / Itunes\"><img src=\"manual/shots/312395099c0ecaa2.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Aqua / Itunes<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/ed17dcb22353fc82.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Game Boy Dark\"><img src=\"manual/shots/ed17dcb22353fc82.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Game Boy Dark<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/7bb11fe11d462092.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Super Nintendo Dark\"><img src=\"manual/shots/7bb11fe11d462092.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Super Nintendo Dark<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c5aa5fe8dc91686d.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Windows 95 Dark\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c5aa5fe8dc91686d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Windows 95 Dark<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/02611e1884ed45db.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Game Boy Color Dark\"><img src=\"manual/shots/02611e1884ed45db.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Game Boy Color Dark<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/2c514ca5750a08ee.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Aqua / Itunes Dark\"><img src=\"manual/shots/2c514ca5750a08ee.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Aqua / Itunes Dark<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/d96eab642b701c22.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Game Boy Dmg\"><img src=\"manual/shots/d96eab642b701c22.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Game Boy Dmg<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/4184d0356b53c3ea.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Game Boy Dmg Dark\"><img src=\"manual/shots/4184d0356b53c3ea.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Game Boy Dmg Dark<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/1c592212490a78c1.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Liquid Glass\"><img src=\"manual/shots/1c592212490a78c1.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Liquid Glass<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/44c9e92ba024bea2.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Liquid Glass Dark\"><img src=\"manual/shots/44c9e92ba024bea2.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Liquid Glass Dark<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/787b243a63de2376.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Lcars\"><img src=\"manual/shots/787b243a63de2376.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Lcars<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/f919580fcb188e94.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Matrix\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f919580fcb188e94.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Matrix<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/a6705b08a29590f5.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Analog\"><img src=\"manual/shots/a6705b08a29590f5.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Analog<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/56d7ed30848a0120.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Flagship\"><img src=\"manual/shots/56d7ed30848a0120.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Flagship<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-theme-families\" data-anchor=\"theme-families\" data-iface=\"classic\">Theme families <span class=\"tag tag--classic\">classic<\/span><\/h4>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Family<\/th><th>Themes<\/th><th>What to expect<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>Modern palettes<\/td><td>ORIGINAL, WHITE, CYBERPUNK, NEON, MOCHA, AURORA, SANDSTONE<\/td><td>Colour schemes on the player's own artwork. ORIGINAL is the player as it ships<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Game Boy<\/td><td>GAME BOY, GAME BOY DARK, GAME BOY COLOR, GAME BOY COLOR DARK, GAME BOY DMG, GAME BOY DMG DARK<\/td><td>Handheld palettes, with their own player artwork and title treatment<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Super Nintendo<\/td><td>SUPER NINTENDO, SUPER NINTENDO DARK<\/td><td>Console colours with their own player artwork<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Windows 95<\/td><td>WINDOWS 95, WINDOWS 95 DARK<\/td><td>Grey bevelled windows and title bars<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Aqua<\/td><td>AQUA / ITUNES, AQUA / ITUNES DARK<\/td><td>Glossy rounded panels<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Liquid Glass<\/td><td>LIQUID GLASS, LIQUID GLASS DARK<\/td><td>Translucent rounded panels<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>LCARS<\/td><td>LCARS<\/td><td>Amber and violet swept panels and capsules. Its own MODS layout with a sidebar<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Matrix<\/td><td>MATRIX<\/td><td>A green terminal with inverse selections and pixel lettering<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Analog<\/td><td>ANALOG<\/td><td>A brushed metal faceplate with lamp keys and switches. Its needle shows the VJ.Tools frame rate, not audio level<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>Most families come in a light and a <strong>DARK<\/strong> version. Pick the dark one for dim booths.<\/p>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--note\"><b>Note<\/b><p>Themes change the screen only. The pad and button lights on the player keep their own colours.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-modern-look\" data-anchor=\"modern-look\" data-iface=\"modern\">MODERN look <span class=\"tag tag--modern\">modern<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>MODERN has one look, <strong>STANDARD<\/strong>, so it has no theme list. The MODS menu is drawn in FLAGSHIP: black pages, a grey section rail and blue selections. More MODERN looks are planned.<\/p>\n<p>Instead of THEME, the SCREEN page offers <strong>LAMPS AND TITLES<\/strong>. Its row shows <strong>ALL SHOWN<\/strong>, or how many parts you have hidden.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Group<\/th><th>Switch or choice<\/th><th>Shown<\/th><th>Hidden<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>TOP BAR<\/td><td>MODE LAMPS<\/td><td>The SINGLE / CONTINUE, A. HOT CUE and A. CUE lamps light while their mode is on<\/td><td>The lamps leave the screen. The modes keep working<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TOP BAR<\/td><td>QUANTIZE LAMP<\/td><td>Each deck's QUANTIZE lamp and beat value above its time<\/td><td>The QUANTIZE button's own light still shows it<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>WAVEFORMS<\/td><td>TITLES IN WAVEFORMS<\/td><td>Track titles inside the waveform lanes<\/td><td>The waveforms use that space. Titles at the bottom stay<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TRACK COLOURS<\/td><td>DECK + WAVE<\/td><td>The colours set for the USB in rekordbox show on the deck tag and its waveform<\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TRACK COLOURS<\/td><td>DECK ONLY<\/td><td>Those colours show on the deck tag only<\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>TRACK COLOURS<\/td><td>OFF<\/td><td>USB colours are not shown<\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>A hidden lamp also stops answering touch.<\/p>\n<p>Your LAMPS AND TITLES choices, TRACK COLOURS and the <strong>BYPASS BUTTON<\/strong> switch are saved to the USB with your other settings, so they come back after the player restarts. So are MODERN's waveform colour, its waveform position and zoom, and how it writes keys.<\/p>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-5\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Every lamp shown\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Every lamp shown<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/f9b6997b34a4582c.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: MODE LAMPS and QUANTIZE LAMP hidden\"><img src=\"manual/shots/f9b6997b34a4582c.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>MODE LAMPS and QUANTIZE LAMP hidden<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/844f5cd9b31a5554.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: TRACK COLOURS DECK + WAVE. Deck 1 comes from a yellow USB set to RGB waveforms, deck 2 from a pink USB\"><img src=\"manual/shots/844f5cd9b31a5554.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>TRACK COLOURS DECK + WAVE. Deck 1 comes from a yellow USB set to RGB waveforms, deck 2 from a pink USB<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/da7b23a580de3b5c.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: TRACK COLOURS DECK ONLY\"><img src=\"manual/shots/da7b23a580de3b5c.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>TRACK COLOURS DECK ONLY<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: TRACK COLOURS OFF\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>TRACK COLOURS OFF<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>The <strong>BYPASS BUTTON<\/strong> switch for MODERN sits with the stem buttons in <strong>STEMS<\/strong>. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-waveform-colours\" data-anchor=\"waveform-colours\">Waveform colours<\/h3>\n<p><strong>WAVEFORM COLOURS<\/strong> sets how the scrolling waveforms are coloured. The setting itself is explained with the rest of the play screen in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"play-screen\">The play screen<\/a>.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Choice<\/th><th>What you see<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>STOCK<\/td><td>The player's own waveform colours<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>RGB<\/td><td>The full-colour waveform. MODERN only<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3-BAND<\/td><td>Lows, mids and highs as layers: lows outside, mids around them, highs at the core. Blue, amber and white unless you choose your own <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\" data-anchor=\"3-band-colours\">3-band colours<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEMS<\/td><td>Drums outside, harmonics around them, vocals at the core, in your stem colours<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>The preview strip on the <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"screen-and-themes\" data-anchor=\"3-band-colours\">3-BAND COLOURS<\/a> page draws the three layers in the colours in use: lows outside, mids around them, highs at the core.<\/p>\n<ul><li>3-BAND and STEMS read the analysis rekordbox and the XZ Mods stem builder already put on the USB. You do not prepare anything extra.<\/li><li>A track without stems shows 3-BAND under STEMS. A track with four stems also shows 3-BAND, because its stems carry no waveform data yet.<\/li><li>Stem colours are set in <strong>STEMS<\/strong> › <strong>STEM COLOURS<\/strong>. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a>.<\/li><li>In MODERN, UTILITY's <strong>WAVEFORM COLOR<\/strong> is the same setting. Your choice is saved to the USB and comes back after a restart.<\/li><\/ul>\n<h3 id=\"m-3-band-colours\" data-anchor=\"3-band-colours\">3-band colours<\/h3>\n<p><strong>3-BAND COLOURS<\/strong> chooses the colour of each band in the 3-BAND waveform: the lows, the mids and the highs. On the SCREEN page it sits beside <strong>THEME<\/strong> in CLASSIC and beside <strong>LAMPS AND TITLES<\/strong> in MODERN. Its row shows the three colours in use.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">MODS · 3-BAND COLOURS<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b621e90b71f0732d.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Every band on STANDARD, the interface&#x27;s own colours.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/85e92095f84da1ea.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Every band on STANDARD, the interface&#x27;s own colours.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"26.500\" data-y=\"13.125\" aria-label=\"1: LOWS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"54.000\" data-y=\"13.125\" aria-label=\"2: MIDS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"82.125\" data-y=\"13.125\" aria-label=\"3: HIGHS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"16.000\" data-y=\"24.583\" aria-label=\"4: STANDARD\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"34.500\" data-y=\"37.083\" aria-label=\"5: Colour choices\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-5\">5<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"6\" data-x=\"58.750\" data-y=\"62.083\" aria-label=\"6: Preview\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-6\">6<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"7\" data-x=\"45.000\" data-y=\"76.458\" aria-label=\"7: RESET 3-BAND COLOURS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-7\">7<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"8\" data-x=\"90.000\" data-y=\"88.542\" aria-label=\"8: WORKS ON\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-8\">8<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>Every band on STANDARD, the interface's own colours.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>LOWS<\/b> <span>The colour of the lows, the outer layer of the waveform.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>MIDS<\/b> <span>The colour of the mids, the middle layer.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>HIGHS<\/b> <span>The colour of the highs, at the core.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>STANDARD<\/b> <span>Keeps the interface's own colour for that band. The highlighted choice in each band is the colour in use.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>Colour choices<\/b> <span>BLUE, RED, GREEN, AMBER, PURPLE, CYAN, PINK and WHITE. Tap one to give it to that band.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"6\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-6\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">6<\/span><div><b>Preview<\/b> <span>A strip drawn the way the 3-BAND waveform stacks the bands, in the colours you chose.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"7\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-7\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">7<\/span><div><b>RESET 3-BAND COLOURS<\/b> <span>Puts all three bands back to STANDARD.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"8\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-6-8\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">8<\/span><div><b>WORKS ON<\/b> <span>3-band colours apply on all four decks.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Open MODS &gt; <strong>SCREEN<\/strong> &gt; <strong>3-BAND COLOURS<\/strong>.<\/li><li>Tap a colour under <strong>LOWS<\/strong>, <strong>MIDS<\/strong> or <strong>HIGHS<\/strong>. Without the touch screen, turn the encoder to a colour and push.<\/li><li>Close MODS to see the play screen in the new colours.<\/li><\/ol>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Band<\/th><th>Choices<\/th><th>Default<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>LOWS<\/td><td>STANDARD, BLUE, RED, GREEN, AMBER, PURPLE, CYAN, PINK, WHITE<\/td><td>STANDARD<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>MIDS<\/td><td>The same nine<\/td><td>STANDARD<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>HIGHS<\/td><td>The same nine<\/td><td>STANDARD<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<ul><li>The colours apply to every 3-BAND waveform: the MODERN lanes and overviews, the CLASSIC scrolling waveform, decks 3 and 4, and the browse preview.<\/li><li>STANDARD is not one fixed colour. It is the colour the interface itself uses for that band, so MODERN and CLASSIC can differ a little.<\/li><li>The 3-BAND pictures under <strong>WAVEFORM COLOURS<\/strong> on the SCREEN page are drawn in your colours too.<\/li><li>Stem colours are separate. Set them in <strong>STEMS<\/strong> › <strong>STEM COLOURS<\/strong>.<\/li><li>The colours are saved to the USB with your other settings.<\/li><\/ul>\n<h3 id=\"m-keys\" data-anchor=\"keys\">Keys<\/h3>\n<h4 id=\"m-key-notation\" data-anchor=\"key-notation\">Key notation<\/h4>\n<p><strong>KEY NOTATION<\/strong> sets how keys are written everywhere MODS draws them: on the play screen, in the track list and in MODS.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Choice<\/th><th>Example<\/th><th>When to use it<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>AS ON THE USB<\/td><td>as set in your library<\/td><td>Keys look the way your rekordbox library writes them<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>MUSICAL<\/td><td>Am<\/td><td>You think in note names<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>WHEEL<\/td><td>8A<\/td><td>You mix by key wheel numbers<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-7\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: MUSICAL. Deck 2 plays Bbm, analysed in Am\"><img src=\"manual/shots/c36b7163962dd08a.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>MUSICAL. Deck 2 plays Bbm, analysed in Am<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/543dad242d6f87b5.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: WHEEL. Deck 2 plays 3A, analysed in 8A\"><img src=\"manual/shots/543dad242d6f87b5.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>WHEEL. Deck 2 plays 3A, analysed in 8A<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<h4 id=\"m-playing-key\" data-anchor=\"playing-key\">Playing key<\/h4>\n<p>With <strong>PLAYING KEY<\/strong> on, each deck shows the key the track plays in now, after tempo changes and key shifts. The original key and the offset in cents sit beside it.<\/p>\n<ul><li>In MODERN the playing key is the big key in each deck's column. Off shows the track's original key there.<\/li><li>In CLASSIC the playing key sits where the beat countdown is. Off brings the countdown back.<\/li><li>Decks 3 and 4 show their playing key too. Until a software deck reports it, the deck shows the track's own key, marked TRACK KEY in CLASSIC.<\/li><\/ul>\n<div class=\"mg\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-8\" data-iface=\"modern\"><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/b501a526a718aa04.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Deck 2 sped up with MT off. It still plays in Am, 38 cents sharp\"><img src=\"manual/shots/b501a526a718aa04.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Deck 2 sped up with MT off. It still plays in Am, 38 cents sharp<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class=\"mg-item\"><button class=\"mg-shot\" type=\"button\" data-zoom=\"manual/shots/8fad872fc7559a67.webp\" data-w=\"800\" data-h=\"480\" aria-label=\"Enlarge: Faster still. Deck 2 now plays in Bbm, and ORIGINAL shows Am\"><img src=\"manual/shots/8fad872fc7559a67.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"><\/button><figcaption>Faster still. Deck 2 now plays in Bbm, and ORIGINAL shows Am<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n<p>The key readout and Key Sync are explained in <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"play-screen\">The play screen<\/a> and <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"performance\">Beat jump and performance features<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h4 id=\"m-key-match-colours-and-key-before-title\" data-anchor=\"key-match-colours-and-key-before-title\">Key match colours and key before title<\/h4>\n<p><strong>KEY MATCH COLOURS<\/strong> colours keys green or amber by how well they mix with the master deck, in the track list and on the play screen. Green means the key mixes with the master's key and sits within 25 cents of it. Amber means it would mix, but it is detuned by more than 25 cents. <strong>KEY BEFORE TITLE<\/strong> puts the key in front of each title in the track list. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"browse\">Browsing and loading<\/a>.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-deck-colours\" data-anchor=\"deck-colours\">Deck colours<\/h3>\n<p>When a screen names a deck, it draws the deck number in a small badge. The badge tells you the deck by its digit and the pair by its colours.<\/p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Decks<\/th><th>Badge<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>1 and 2<\/td><td>White digit on grey<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>3 and 4<\/td><td>Black digit on white<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>A deck that is not live<\/td><td>The same badge, dimmed<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>\n<p>No deck owns a colour. Blue and pale blue mark the deck a side of the player controls. Amber, red, green, the waveform bands and USB colours keep their own meanings. The <strong>WORKS ON<\/strong> row in the MODS dock uses the same badges, in mixer order <strong>3 1 2 4<\/strong>. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a> for the deck view.<\/p>\n<h3 id=\"m-system-readout\" data-anchor=\"system-readout\">System readout<\/h3>\n<p><strong>SYSTEM READOUT<\/strong> puts CPU load, memory and temperature beside <strong>STEMS<\/strong> and <strong>MODS<\/strong> on the top bar. Open it to see deck 3 and 4 audio render times and active key shifters across all four decks. P99 is the time at or below which 99% of the last 256 rendered blocks finished; MAX is the longest. Short blocks are scaled to a full block. D3+D4 MAX adds both maxima and compares them with the 5,805 microseconds available per block. New shifts use a stricter 3,483 microsecond budget, leaving time for other work. These render numbers include decoding, time stretch and key shift; they do not measure the complete output path. Use them when you suspect the player is working hard, for example with stems on both decks and four decks running.<\/p>\n<figure class=\"mf\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-9\"><div class=\"mf-frame\"><div class=\"mf-bar\"><span class=\"mf-label\">SYSTEM READOUT<\/span><\/div><div class=\"mf-stage\"><img src=\"manual/shots/33f35640dc496caf.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The first setup step with live readings and four key shifters engaged.\" data-iface=\"modern\"><img src=\"manual/shots/e3301f8ee8f7c8fd.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"480\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"The first setup step with live readings and four key shifters engaged.\" data-iface=\"classic\"><span class=\"mf-spot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><\/span><div class=\"mf-marks\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Numbered points on the picture\"><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"1\" data-x=\"28.125\" data-y=\"21.875\" aria-label=\"1: STEP\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-1\">1<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"2\" data-x=\"55.000\" data-y=\"42.917\" aria-label=\"2: What the numbers mean\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-2\">2<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"3\" data-x=\"53.750\" data-y=\"53.125\" aria-label=\"3: Audio render time\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-3\">3<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"4\" data-x=\"53.750\" data-y=\"58.750\" aria-label=\"4: Key shifters\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-4\">4<\/button><button class=\"mf-mark\" type=\"button\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-n=\"5\" data-x=\"87.500\" data-y=\"74.167\" aria-label=\"5: DETECT METRICS\" aria-describedby=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-5\">5<\/button><\/div><\/div><\/div><figcaption>The first setup step with live readings and four key shifters engaged.<\/figcaption><ol class=\"mf-legend\" aria-label=\"What the numbers show\"><li data-n=\"1\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-1\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">1<\/span><div><b>STEP<\/b> <span>Where you are in the setup.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"2\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-2\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">2<\/span><div><b>What the numbers mean<\/b> <span>CPU 100% means all four cores are busy. RAM leaves out cache. 80 C turns yellow, 90 C flashes red with HOT.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"3\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-3\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">3<\/span><div><b>Audio render time<\/b> <span>Each software deck shows its p99 and maximum render time in microseconds. LAST RUN means the reading is no longer live.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"4\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-4\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">4<\/span><div><b>Key shifters<\/b> <span>Counts shifted decks, including decks 1 and 2. The combined software maximum is shown against one audio block.<\/span><\/div><\/li><li data-n=\"5\" id=\"f-screen-and-themes-9-5\"><span class=\"mf-chip\" aria-hidden=\"true\">5<\/span><div><b>DETECT METRICS<\/b> <span>Runs the current step. Push to move through the setup.<\/span><\/div><\/li><\/ol><\/figure>\n<ol class=\"steps\"><li>Choose <strong>SYSTEM READOUT<\/strong> on the SCREEN page.<\/li><li>Push <strong>DETECT METRICS<\/strong>. The setup looks for CPU, memory and the temperature sensor.<\/li><li>Follow the remaining steps until the live readings show.<\/li><\/ol>\n<p>After setup the row on the SCREEN page reads <strong>ON<\/strong>. On the top bar, <strong>METRICS STARTING - TAP TO SET UP<\/strong> means the readings have not arrived yet. <strong>METRICS STALE - TAP TO VERIFY<\/strong> means they stopped updating. Tap either one to open the setup again.<\/p>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--note\"><b>Note<\/b><p>Only the temperature of the main chip is available on the XDJ-XZ.<\/p><\/aside>\n<h3 id=\"m-when-something-looks-wrong\" data-anchor=\"when-something-looks-wrong\">When something looks wrong<\/h3>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>What you see<\/th><th>What to do<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>The theme did not change<\/td><td>Close MODS. The play screen takes the new theme once MODS is closed<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>DECK VIEW is missing from SCREEN<\/td><td>This player's USB loader cannot run decks 3 and 4. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"four-decks\">Four decks<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>STEMS waveforms look like 3-BAND<\/td><td>The track has no prepared stems, or it has four stems. See <a class=\"m-link\" href=\"#manual\" data-chapter=\"stems\">Stems<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Keys show in the wrong notation<\/td><td>Set KEY NOTATION. AS ON THE USB follows your library's own setting<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>The waveform colours are not the ones you expect<\/td><td>Check 3-BAND COLOURS. RESET 3-BAND COLOURS puts every band back to STANDARD<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div>";
